# 578 frame-map id	name  -- a rig ("base" skeleton, index 1 / FRAME_MAPS).
# A seq's frames pack a frame-group id in the high 16 bits; that group's frames carry a
# FrameType.frameMapId, and THAT is the rig. Everything sharing a rig animates the same
# skeleton, and nothing else can play those seqs -- the frame group is narrower (the human
# rig alone spans groups 207, 1868 and many more, all frame map 0).
# Names are derived, not stored: the cache holds no name hash for index 1. They come from
# the seq names on the rig (dumps/578/gameval/seq.sym) plus the display names of the npcs
# and locs that reach it. See rig.tsv for the grade and the evidence behind each one, and
# dumps/578/anim-skeleton-gfx-relations.txt for the full membership of every rig.
# `name#N` means several rigs derived the same name; #1 (the largest) drops the suffix.
